---
description: Layering, state and structure rules for Dart code
globs: lib/**/*.dart
alwaysApply: false
---

- Dependency direction: `ui -> providers/controllers -> repositories -> data`. A feature never imports another feature's `ui/`.
- Widgets only render `AsyncValue`s and call controller or repository methods. No business rules, no Drift queries, no `DateTime.now()` (use `nowProvider`).
- State is Riverpod (ADR-0001): `StreamProvider` for database reads, `Notifier` for UI-only state, plain classes for repositories. Never `ref.read` inside `build`. Repository providers are not auto-disposed.
- Undo callbacks run from SnackBars that outlive screens: capture the repository before navigating.
- Do not add a domain layer, repository interfaces, freezed, json_serializable or any other state library (ADR-0003).
- Prefer `const`, small widgets and narrow `ref.watch` scopes. Split files before they pass about 300 lines.
- Folder layout follows `docs/architecture.md` section 2.3.
